---
const synonyms = [
  ["happy", "joyful, glad, content, cheerful"],
  ["brave", "courageous, bold, fearless"],
  ["big", "large, huge, enormous, gigantic"]
];

const antonyms = [
  ["tidy", "messy"],
  ["generous", "mean"],
  ["scarce", "plentiful"],
  ["agree", "disagree"]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Synonyms and Antonyms - Similar and opposite</h1>
  <section class="summary-block summary-sand">
    <h2>Synonyms</h2>
    <p>A synonym has the same meaning, or nearly the same meaning.</p>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Word</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Synonyms</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          synonyms.map(([word, matches]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{word}</th>
              <td>{matches}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>“Which word means the same as <em>brave</em>?” In “He was a <em>valiant</em> soldier”, <em>valiant</em> means <strong>brave</strong>.</p>
    <p>Learn the shade of meaning. <em>Angry</em> is not <em>furious</em>: furious is the stronger feeling.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-mint">
    <h2>Antonyms</h2>
    <p>An antonym has the opposite meaning.</p>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Word</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Antonym</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          antonyms.map(([word, opposite]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{word}</th>
              <td>{opposite}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>“Which word is the opposite of <em>honest</em>?”</p>
    <p>A prefix can flip the meaning: <em>un-</em> (happy → unhappy), <em>dis-</em> (agree → disagree), and <em>in-</em>, <em>im-</em>, <em>il-</em> or <em>ir-</em> (possible → impossible).</p>
  </section>
</div>
